  "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-16(0)-6y-91 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-6y-91 & =0 \\\\ (y-13)(y+7) & =0 \\\\ y & =13,-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $y$-axis at $(0,13)$ and $(0,-7).$",
